```

---

## Document Types

### Technical Report
- Cover page with title, author, date, version
- Table of contents
- Executive summary
- Sections: Introduction, Architecture, Implementation, Results, Conclusion
- Diagrams: architecture diagrams, data charts
- Code listings, tables

### Developer CV / Resume
- Compact 1–2 page layout
- Two-column header (name/title left, contact right)
- Sections: Summary, Experience, Skills, Education, Projects
- Skill bars using TikZ
- No cover page

### Research Paper
- IEEE or ACM-inspired layout
- Abstract block
- Sections: Abstract, Introduction, Related Work, Methodology, Results, Discussion, Conclusion
- References section with `\bibliography`
- Figures with captions

### Architecture Document
- System context diagram (top-level)
- Component diagrams per layer
- Sequence diagrams for key flows
- Data flow diagrams
- Decision tables

---

## Compilation Script

Use this Python helper to compile reliably:

```python
import subprocess, shutil, os

def compile_latex(tex_path: str, output_dir: str = "/mnt/user-data/outputs") -> str:
    """Compile a .tex file to PDF, run twice for cross-references."""
    work_dir = os.path.dirname(tex_path)
    base = os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(tex_path))[0]
    cmd = ["pdflatex", "-interaction=nonstopmode", "-halt-on-error",
           "-output-directory", work_dir, tex_path]

    for run in range(2):           # Two passes for TOC / refs
        result = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, cwd=work_dir)
        if result.returncode != 0:
            # Surface the first LaTeX error
            for line in result.stdout.splitlines():
                if line.startswith("!"):
                    raise RuntimeError(f"LaTeX error (pass {run+1}): {line}")

    pdf_src = os.path.join(work_dir, f"{base}.pdf")
    os.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)
    pdf_dst = os.path.join(output_dir, f"{base}.pdf")
    shutil.copy2(pdf_src, pdf_dst)
    return pdf_dst
```

---

## Quality Checklist

Before delivering any PDF, verify:

- [ ] Color theme applied consistently (headings, rules, links)
- [ ] Cover page present for reports/papers (not CVs)
- [ ] Table of contents generated (reports/papers only)
- [ ] Header/footer active on all pages
- [ ] Diagrams render without errors
- [ ] Code blocks use listings style
- [ ] Tables use booktabs (`\toprule`, `\midrule`, `\bottomrule`)
- [ ] Compiled **twice** (cross-references resolved)
- [ ] PDF delivered via `present_files`

---

## Error Recovery

| Error | Fix |
|---|---|
| `Undefined control sequence` | Check package is loaded; add `\usepackage{...}` |
| `Missing $ inserted` | Math content outside `$...$` or `\[...\]` |
| TikZ compile hang | Add `\usetikzlibrary` for required libs |
| Overfull `\hbox` | Add `\sloppy` or break long strings |
| Missing font | Fall back to `lmodern` and `\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}` |
| PGFPlots axis error | Set `\pgfplotsset{compat=1.18}` |
| Hyperref conflicts | Load `hyperref` **last** in preamble |

---

